// The (192,32) pair-indexed feed tables, written exactly as the generic renderer
// will declare them: derived from the public eight-byte stripe record, page
// contained, one index per renderer pair.
//
// This is a PROBE fixture, not a renderer.  It exists so the feed's origin can be
// proved by building the real thing and reading the emitted ROM bytes, rather than
// by reasoning about a table nobody has compiled:
//
//   * stripe_generic_feed_source_bound.pl owns the layout these tables encode and
//     checks that the bytes below match it.
//   * test/vcs_all_five_stripe_feed_tables.pl builds the file, checks the ROM
//     bytes, the page containment, and the index coverage.
//
// Y = region-1-q indexes pair q of the region, and region is 96 pairs at 192 lines
// with 32 stripes of three pairs each.  So Y counts 95..0 and the read at pair q is
// feedN[Y].  There is no stripe index and no division anywhere: which record field
// lands in which slot is decided here, at build time.
//
// The three tables are 288 bytes and cost nothing at run time.  feed2's
// pair-2 slots are unused, which is why it is 96 bytes rather than 64.
include "vcs.c26"

// Logical record per stripe: C0, C1, PF0, PF1, PF2, PF3, PF4, PF5.
